<h2 class="h2" data-split>Your retail scheduling questions, answered</h2>
<p class="txt">Still have questions? We'll walk you through it with your own scheduling rules.</p>
</div>
<div class="retail-faq" data-retail-faq style="flex:2 1 520px;min-width:0" data-reveal>
<details><summary>What is retail scheduling software?</summary><p>Retail scheduling software builds employee schedules around expected customer demand instead of fixed shift templates. Workofo forecasts workload per store in 15-minute intervals, applies labor rules and skills, and creates optimized schedules automatically.</p></details>
<details><summary>How does Workofo handle scheduling across multiple stores?</summary><p>Workofo plans staffing per location and lets you lend or borrow employees between stores to cover absences and demand spikes. Long-term cross-location staffing can be automated.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is Workofo suitable for large retail chains?</summary><p>Yes. Workofo is built to scale, from specialty retailers to chains with 20,000 or more employees, with demand forecasting, automated scheduling and integration with HR and payroll systems.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Workofo integrate with POS, HR and payroll systems?</summary><p>Yes. Workofo connects to your existing HR, payroll and POS systems, so sales and volume data feed the forecast and approved schedules flow back to payroll.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is there an app for retail employee scheduling?</summary><p>Yes. The Workofo app for iOS and Android lets employees view schedules, submit preferences and swap shifts, and lets managers approve requests on the go.</p></details>
<div class="retail-faq__more" data-retail-faq-more hidden>
<details><summary>How is Workofo different from a basic retail scheduling app?</summary><p>Workofo starts with demand forecasting and builds shifts around it. Its retail workforce management approach brings contracts, skills and availability into the same calculation, helping you find options that fixed patterns can miss.</p></details>
<details><summary>How does Workofo forecast retail demand?</summary><p>It uses the drivers that define work in your stores, such as sales, volumes, tasks or service targets, and forecasts staffing needs down to 15-minute intervals per location.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can Workofo handle labor law and union agreements?</summary><p>Yes. Contracts, rest rules, skills and local agreements are encoded into every schedule so managers are not left checking compliance by hand.</p></details>
<details><summary>How much capacity can we unlock?</summary><p>That depends on your stores. Better allocation can put more hours into busy periods, reduce overtime or help another location. We assess the opportunity against your demand and scheduling rules.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do managers stay in control of the schedule?</summary><p>Yes. Workofo builds the plan; managers review, adjust and publish. Automation handles the heavy lifting, not the final call.</p></details>
</div>
<button type="button" class="pill retail-faq-more__toggle" data-retail-faq-toggle aria-expanded="false">
<span class="retail-faq-more__more">Load more questions</span>
<span class="retail-faq-more__less">Show less</span>
<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
</button>
</div>
